---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import { LINKEDIN_URL, SCHEDULING_LINK } from '../consts';

const influences = [
	{
		name: 'Shape Up',
		href: 'https://basecamp.com/shapeup',
		note: 'from Basecamp. Fixed time, variable scope. It’s why the budget is fixed and the scope moves.',
	},
	{
		name: 'The Lean Startup',
		href: 'https://theleanstartup.com/',
		note: 'Eric Ries. The experiment as the unit of work.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Design thinking',
		href: 'https://designthinking.ideo.com/',
		note: 'as IDEO teaches it. Put the thing in real hands before you trust your own opinion of it.',
	},
	{
		name: 'Pivotal Labs',
		href: 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pivotal_Labs',
		note: 'A team learns all of this by doing it next to someone for a few months.',
	},
];
---

<MarketingLayout
	title="Work | People Purpose Product"
	description="Fractional product ownership and product owner coaching for mission-driven teams, and what a typical month looks like."
>
	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="measure page-header">
			<h1>Work</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				I work as the product owner for teams that have funding and a real problem, and
				either nobody in the seat or someone in it who's never been shown the craft. Here's
				what that looks like, and how to tell if it fits.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap services">
		<div class="label ruled">How we work together</div>

		<article class="service">
			<div class="service-head">
				<h2>Fractional product owner</h2>
				<p class="fit"><b>Fits when</b> you already have engineers, and nobody deciding what they build.</p>
				<p class="fit"><b>Does not fit when</b> you have a mature backlog and want a technical product manager to run it. That's a different hire, and I'll say so on the call.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="service-body">
				<p>
					The roadmap stays yours. I take the product owner seat on your team and sit in the
					meetings: drafting the requirements, designing the experiments, reading what comes
					back, making the call with your people in the room.
				</p>
				<p>
					A product manager who runs the product day to day is table stakes. The part that's
					harder to find is ownership: deciding what gets built, in what order, and standing
					behind the call. I do both.
				</p>
			</div>
		</article>

		<article class="service">
			<div class="service-head">
				<h2>Product owner coaching</h2>
				<p class="fit"><b>Fits when</b> someone on your team has the instincts and has never had anyone to learn the craft from.</p>
				<p class="fit"><b>Does not fit when</b> nobody on the team has time in the seat. The coaching is the doing, so the person needs hours, not just interest.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="service-body">
				<p>
					For the person already doing this job without the title. We draft the roadmap
					together, run the experiments together, and sit in it together when an idea
					flops. Then you keep doing it after I'm gone.
				</p>
			</div>
		</article>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="measure month">
			<h2>What a typical month looks like</h2>
			<p>
				I can do it for you. I can teach you how. What works best is doing it with you.
			</p>
			<ol class="steps">
				<li>A 30-minute call. You tell me what you're working on.</li>
				<li>I sit in on how your product work runs today. One or two meetings.</li>
				<li>We draft the roadmap together.</li>
				<li>We write the requirements for the first build, and the experiment that tells us whether it helped.</li>
				<li>Engineering builds it. We put it in real hands fast.</li>
				<li>We read what came back together, and we make the call: keep it, change it, or drop it.</li>
				<li>Steps 4 to 6 repeat. The goal is one experiment a week.</li>
			</ol>
			<p>
				Step 6 is the part people skip, and it's the part that pays. A client wanted a
				chatbot to handle one step of their flow. We looked at what came back together and
				realized a plain form would do that job correctly every single time. That's a
				smaller product than the one we started with, and a better one.
			</p>
			<p>
				Engagements run month to month. Each month we size the work to your budget. The
				scope moves. The invoice does not.
			</p>
			<div class="lists">
				<div class="list">
					<h3>What you get</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>A roadmap: what to build, in what order, and why.</li>
						<li>Requirements for each build, written so engineering can build it once.</li>
						<li>An experiment design for each build, so we know whether it helped.</li>
						<li>A readout after each experiment: what we saw, and what we do next.</li>
						<li>An evidence record a funder can read.</li>
						<li>A team that can run this loop after I'm gone.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="list">
					<h3>What I need from you</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>One person who can meet weekly, get the right people in the room, and drive a decision.</li>
						<li>A way to put the product in front of the people it serves.</li>
						<li>Engineers, or an introduction to some I've worked with.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p>
				Every engagement ends the same way. Your team runs steps 3 to 6 without me.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="measure influences">
			<h2>Where this comes from</h2>
			<p>My school of product ownership had many teachers. A few I keep going back to:</p>
			<ul>
				{influences.map((i) => (
					<li><a href={i.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{i.name}</a>, {i.note}</li>
				))}
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap">
		<div class="measure closing">
			<h2>Let's talk</h2>
			<p>
				If any of this resonates, I'd love to talk. Book 30 minutes and tell me what
				you're working on.
			</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="primary" href={SCHEDULING_LINK} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Find a time &rarr;</a>
				<span class="aside">Prefer email? Write me at <a class="email-link" href={LINKEDIN_URL}>hello at this domain</a>.</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</MarketingLayout>

<script>
	// Assemble the address in the browser so scrapers reading the raw HTML
	// never see a complete email. The href above is a fallback (LinkedIn)
	// for the rare no-JS visitor.
	const user = 'hello';
	const domain = 'peoplepurposeproduct.com';
	const address = `${user}@${domain}`;
	document.querySelectorAll('.email-link').forEach((el) => {
		el.setAttribute('href', `mailto:${address}`);
		el.textContent = address;
	});
</script>

<style>
	.page-header {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 24px;
		padding: 96px 0 56px;
	}
	.lede {
		font-size: 22px;
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: var(--body);
	}

	.services {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		padding-bottom: 32px;
	}
	.service {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 250px minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 40px;
		align-items: start;
		padding: 26px 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-light);
	}
	.service-head {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 10px;
	}
	.service-head h2 {
		font-size: 26px;
		line-height: 1.2;
	}
	.fit {
		font-size: 16px;
		line-height: 1.45;
		color: var(--muted);
	}
	.service-body {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 12px;
	}
	.service-body p {
		font-size: 18px;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--body);
	}

	.month,
	.influences {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 18px;
		padding: 32px 0 56px;
	}
	.month p,
	.influences p,
	.closing p {
		font-size: 19px;
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--body);
	}
	.steps {
		padding-left: 1.4em;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 8px;
		font-size: 19px;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--body);
	}
	.lists {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 40px;
		padding-top: 8px;
	}
	.list {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 10px;
	}
	.list h3 {
		font-size: 20px;
	}
	.list ul,
	.influences ul {
		padding-left: 1.2em;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 8px;
		font-size: 17px;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--body-soft);
	}
	.influences ul {
		font-size: 19px;
		color: var(--body);
	}
	.influences {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
		padding-top: 48px;
	}

	.closing {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 18px;
		padding: 48px 0 72px;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.page-header {
			padding: 48px 0 40px;
			gap: 18px;
		}
		.lede {
			font-size: 20px;
		}
		.service {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 14px;
			padding: 22px 0;
		}
		.service-head h2 {
			font-size: 24px;
		}
		.month,
		.influences {
			padding: 24px 0 48px;
		}
		.lists {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 24px;
		}
		.closing {
			padding: 40px 0 56px;
		}
	}
</style>
